# Trivy CVE allowlist for @usetheo/memory standalone image.
#
# Format (mirror of .claude/rules/deps-audit-allowlist.txt):
#   CVE-ID|REASON|SUNSET-DATE
#
# Sunset discipline per .claude/rules/deps-audit-golden-rule.md:
#   - CRITICAL CVEs: sunset ≤ 30 days
#   - HIGH CVEs:     sunset ≤ 60 days
#   - MEDIUM CVEs:   sunset ≤ 90 days
#
# Lines beginning with `#` are comments (Trivy treats them as ignored).
# Each non-comment line must be a bare CVE ID (the pipe-delimited fields
# above are stripped before Trivy reads the file — see scripts hook in
# the docker-publish workflow if/when the allowlist needs entries).
#
# At v0.1.0-alpha this file is intentionally EMPTY — no production CVE
# has been allowlisted yet. New entries require a sunset date written
# next to the CVE ID on the SAME line via a `# sunset: YYYY-MM-DD` trailing
# comment for human review.
#
# @see Plan theo-memory-standalone-p0 § T3.3 + EC-43
# @see .claude/rules/deps-audit-golden-rule.md § Severity rubric
